# Kebu ecosystem (Phase One law)

Full human reference: `docs/KEBU-ECOSYSTEM.md`.

This map keeps engineering compatible with future products. **It is not permission to build them now.**

## Audience & personality

Primary audience: **African youth** (students, first-time founders, freelancers, creators, informal and small-business owners, people with ideas but little money or no coding experience).

Do **not** design like traditional enterprise software. Explain incorporation, hosting, domains, APIs, analytics, cash flow, compliance, trade, etc. in plain language; give advanced users deeper controls.

Feel: ambitious, youthful, intelligent, African, encouraging, energetic, creative, modern, practical, trustworthy, easy to understand, serious enough for real businesses.

Must **not** feel: childish, cold corporate, government portal, accounting software, generic Western SaaS, AI-chatbox pile, textbook, distraction social feed.

Users should feel: **“I can actually build this.”**

## Core product principle

Every major experience answers one or more of: What opportunity exists? What can I build? How? Who can help? How do I launch / register / sell / get paid / understand / grow / trade / learn missing skills?

Every screen must clarify the **next action**. No dashboards that only display data.

## Phase One only (current product)

**Phase One** = Africa’s AI Business Builder and Opportunity Operating System. This is the only ecosystem product under full implementation.

Help users: discover → understand → create business → Kebu ID → register/prepare → website/store → AI generate/improve → publish/host → sell → payments (incl. K21 where available) → analytics → next actions → improve over time.

Phase One systems (build only when assigned as slices): Kebu AI · Opportunity OS · Build My Country · business creation/registration · Kebu ID · Kebu Score (KA Score) · website AI/templates/editor · store/orders/payments · hosting/domains · analytics · AI guidance · business news when assigned.

Do **not** expand Phase One into unrelated productivity or infrastructure systems unless explicitly assigned.

## Kebu AI

Intelligent assistant tied to the user’s businesses, projects, websites, stores, products, orders, analytics, opportunities, goals, research, learning — with **RBAC and business boundaries**. Never a general chatbot only. Never access another user’s private business data.

## Opportunity OS & news

Opportunity OS: discover what to build; trust labels mandatory (Verified / public-source / Estimated / AI-generated / Requires validation). “Build This Opportunity” → connected business journey.

Business news (working names only — do not finalize): Kebu Pulse / Today / Business / Opportunities / Brief. Youth-oriented; every story → implications + opportunity to research/build. No unsupported claims. **Do not build unless assigned.**

## Kebu Score (= KA Score)

Business score on a Kebu ID. Explainable: helping/hurting factors, missing data, actions, confidence, history. Not popularity. Not purchasable. Not initially an official regulated credit score. See `kebu-ka-score.mdc`.

## Future products (compatibility only — do not build)

| Product | Role | Phase One rule |
|--------|------|----------------|
| **Kebu Cloud** | Broader app deploy/hosting (not Phase One site hosting) | Do not build |
| **Kebu Studio** | Design / brand / packaging canvas | Basic branding OK; no Canva-style editor |
| **Kebu Learn** | Project-based education | Guidance OK; no full LMS |
| **Kebu Docs** | Docs/sheets/slides suite | Downloadable reports OK; no office suite |
| **Kebu Labs** | Research arm feeding Opportunity OS | Architecture for sources OK; no institution CMS |
| **Kebu Ventures** | Incubation / investment (legally separate) | Score may flag readiness; never auto-fund |
| **Talent / work network** | Cofounders, hire, teams | Optimize for work done; no social feed |

Shared later: account, profile, business memberships, Kebu ID, permissions, billing, notifications, AI infra, design system, audit, security — **separate product domains**, not one giant table/nav.

Possible domains: identity · business · opportunity · websites · commerce · analytics · registration · cloud · design · learning · productivity · research · investment · talent.

## Youth UX / affordability / mobile

Clear language · explain terms · show progress · next step · autosave where appropriate · mobile-first · fewer forms · examples/templates · celebrate real progress without childishness.

Affordability: free/low-cost/student/pay-as-you-go · regional payments · K21 · AI cost controls. Do not assume credit cards, expensive devices, or reliable broadband.

Mobile & connectivity: compressed assets · progressive load · efficient APIs · autosave queues · retry · local drafts only when honest · never fake “saved” for unsynced local-only data.

## Strict future-product rule

When implementing Phase One:

- Do not build Cloud / Studio / Docs / Learn / Ventures / Labs / talent network merely because they appear here.
- No unfinished pages, placeholder dashboards, empty nav, “Coming Soon”, fake integrations, empty unused tables, or buttons that lead nowhere unless explicitly requested.
- Do not let future products distract from the **assigned vertical slice**.

## Recommended Phase One order (one slice at a time)

Audit → auth → profile → Kebu ID → roles → business dashboard → registration prep/modules/progress → website templates → create from template → AI generation → visual editor → autosave/versions → publish → subdomains → custom domains → store → products → cart → checkout → orders → K21 → store analytics events → analytics dashboard → AI business intelligence → Kebu Score → Opportunity country → resource/import → Opportunity AI → Build This Opportunity → business news.

Never multiple major slices in parallel. See `kebu-single-slice.mdc` / `kebu-vertical-slice.mdc`.

## Success test

A young African user can say they found an opportunity, understood it, created and registered a business, built and launched a site/store, got a customer, understood analytics, improved, found people to build with, and learned by creating something real.
